# Next.js / React UI

## App structure

- App Router only (`src/app`). No Pages Router.
- Use `'use client'` when the file needs state, effects, or browser APIs (see `@src/app/page.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/navbar.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/chatbot.tsx`).
- Put new UI under `src/app/components/ui/` unless introducing a clearer feature folder by request.
- Page composition: sticky `Navbar` → `Hero` (intro + `Chatbot`) → `ExperienceTimeline` → `SkillsGrid` → `AboutSection` (includes `ThemePicker`) → `SiteFooter`, wrapped in `ThemeProvider` then `ChatProvider`.
- Backend Route Handlers live under `src/app/api/v1/` (not in the UI tree); keep secrets and LLM/DB work out of client components.

## Styling

- Tailwind + existing shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `ScrollArea`).
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (`@src/lib/utils.ts`).
- Use themeable `surface-*` / `glow` tokens (`bg-surface-950`, `bg-surface-900/60` cards, glow accent). Never hardcode `zinc-*`.
- Themes: `html[data-theme]` from `@src/shared/themes.ts` via `ThemeProvider`; backgrounds in `@src/app/components/ui/backgrounds/`. Default theme is `default` (original look); album picks toggle off to revert.
- Use `ScrollArea` for dark-themed scroll regions; keep `color-scheme: dark` on `html`.
- Skill logos come from `@src/shared/skillIcons.ts` (`simple-icons`); do not reintroduce per-skill local SVGs for the skills grid unless requested.
- `components.json` may alias utils to `@/app/lib/utils`; the real file is `@/lib/utils`. Do not duplicate `utils.ts` to “fix” the alias.

## State and exports

- Prefer local `useState` / `useRef` / `useEffect`. Do not add a global store unless justified.
- Chat thread state lives in `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts` and is shared via `@src/app/components/ui/chat-provider.tsx` (`useChat`) so sibling sections (e.g. experience) can call `sendMessage`.
- Theme selection lives in `@src/app/components/ui/theme-provider.tsx` (`useTheme` / `toggleAlbumTheme`) and persists album picks to `localStorage` (cleared on default).
- Match surrounding export style (named for `Chatbot`, hooks, primitives; default where the file already defaults).

## Chat UX invariants

Canonical UI: `@src/app/components/ui/chatbot.tsx`. State/streaming: `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts`.

- Render assistant markdown with `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm`
- Stream by appending content chunks to the assistant bubble
- Thread with `parent_id` / server `assistant_message_id`
- Ctrl/Cmd+K clears the thread via `@src/hooks/refreshChatKeyHandler.ts`
- Autoscroll the message container (`scrollTop`), not the whole page (`scrollIntoView`)
- Do not call Telegram (or other side-effect notify APIs) after stream completion

## Profile content

- Client-facing copy, experience, skills, and nav links: `@src/shared/profile.ts`
- LLM background facts: `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` (the bot is Daniel's assistant; speak about him in the third person)
- When updating jobs/education/location, update both files so UI and chat stay consistent

## Resume

- Resume is a static asset at `/resume.pdf` (navbar and footer download links). Do not add a custom resume API route unless requested.
